{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784023045,"nonce":"jHbMN+fhKLj4LuAqrtKp5rArWiM=","title":"The `invoke` step kind and its **compile-time inlining** for a single local `.scarab/lib/` pipeline (ADR-0038). An author writes a step `invoke: ./lib/deploy.yaml`; at compile the referenced pipeline's steps are flattened into the caller's DAG — there is no runtime \"sub-pipeline\" object. Inlined step ids are namespaced by the invoke-step id (`deploy/build`) and `needs` edges are rewritten across the seam.","message":"Because compile is pure (ADR-0031), the pure compiler must receive the lib sources rather than perform I/O: the server's trigger path pre-fetches `.scarab/**` via `ForgePort` and passes a `{path -\u003e source}` map to a resolver-based compile entrypoint. The lib path is repo-relative and read at the caller's ref.\n\nPath safety ships with the feature: reject absolute paths, `../` traversal out of the repo tree, and cross-repo references at compile with a clear diagnostic (cross-repo is `on: upstream`, not `invoke`).\n\nSingle level only in this slice (recursion/nesting, matrix, and the typed inputs/outputs interface are follow-ups).\n\n\n- [ ] `invoke:` step kind exists in the IR and YAML frontend; validated at compile.\n- [ ] A pure compile entrypoint accepts a `{path -\u003e source}` map of `.scarab/**` and resolves an `invoke` by inlining the referenced pipeline's steps.\n- [ ] Inlined step ids are namespaced by the invoke-step id (`deploy/build`); `needs` edges rewrite correctly across the seam; the result is a single valid flat DAG.\n- [ ] Path resolution is repo-relative and read at the caller's ref; absolute paths, `../` escape, and cross-repo refs are rejected at compile with diagnostics.\n- [ ] The server trigger path fetches the lib sources and passes them to compile; a triggered run's persisted DAG contains the flattened, namespaced steps.\n- [ ] A pipeline file under `.scarab/lib/` is NOT triggered as a top-level pipeline (it exists only to be invoked).\n- [ ] Tests cover: happy-path inline + namespacing, needs-rewrite, each path-safety rejection, and the lib-not-triggered rule. Suite green vs local Postgres.\n\n\nNone - can start immediately.","files":null}]}